<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12673" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēfenso</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a. intens.</i> [defendo].
			*</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To fend off diligently, ward off</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">metus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 2, 105</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To defend diligently, protect</i> (rare; mostly
			ante-class. and <b>poet.</b>, not in Cic. or
			Caes.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moenia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 3, 3, 30</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 26, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">60, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alios ab hostibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 97</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humeros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 376</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se ipsa moenia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 45</span></i>
			 (al. defendebant): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se injuria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 3, 3, 39</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dum defensamus (sc. armentum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 11, 374</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
